The question asks whether inside {{ }} in Twig you can call arbitrary PHP code directly.

In Twig, {{ }} is used for outputting variables and expressions. You can call methods on objects (e.g., {{ foo.bar() })), but you cannot write arbitrary PHP code like {{ $obj->method($param) }} or {{ array_map(fn, $arr) }} or use PHP operators beyond what Twig supports (like the ternary operator in a limited form, comparison operators, etc.).

Twig has its own expression language. You can:
